    {
      "id": 17,
      "title": "Set up E2ETesting Plugin Foundation with Required Dependencies",
      "description": "Create the basic structure for the E2ETesting plugin following PenPal's plugin architecture patterns, with dependencies on CoreAPI, Docker, and JobsTracker plugins.",
      "details": "Implement the foundation for the E2ETesting plugin with the following components:\n\n1. Create `manifest.json` with:\n   - Plugin name: 'E2ETesting'\n   - Version information\n   - Dependencies explicitly listed: CoreAPI, Docker, and JobsTracker\n   - Any required permissions\n\n2. Create `index.js` that:\n   - Exports the plugin class\n   - Handles proper module exports\n\n3. Create `plugin.js` that:\n   - Defines the E2ETesting plugin class\n   - Implements the standard plugin lifecycle methods (register, load, start, stop)\n   - Sets up proper dependency injection for CoreAPI, Docker, and JobsTracker\n   - Follows PenPal's established plugin registration pattern\n\n4. Set up the GraphQL schema structure:\n   - Create a `schema` directory\n   - Implement basic type definitions in `schema/typeDefs.js`\n   - Implement basic resolvers in `schema/resolvers.js`\n   - Ensure the schema is properly exported and registered with the GraphQL server\n\n5. Create a basic README.md documenting:\n   - The plugin's purpose\n   - Dependencies\n   - Basic usage instructions\n\nEnsure all files follow the project's coding standards and patterns established in other plugins.",
      "testStrategy": "Verify the plugin foundation is correctly implemented through the following tests:\n\n1. **Plugin Registration Test**:\n   - Verify the plugin registers successfully with the PenPal framework\n   - Confirm no errors during the registration process\n   - Check that dependencies are correctly specified and loaded\n\n2. **Structure Validation**:\n   - Validate all required files exist (manifest.json, index.js, plugin.js, schema files)\n   - Verify the manifest.json contains correct dependencies on CoreAPI, Docker, and JobsTracker\n   - Ensure the plugin class properly extends the base Plugin class\n\n3. **GraphQL Schema Test**:\n   - Verify the GraphQL schema can be parsed without errors\n   - Test that the schema is properly registered with the GraphQL server\n   - Run a simple introspection query to confirm the schema is accessible\n\n4. **Dependency Injection Test**:\n   - Verify the plugin correctly receives and can access the CoreAPI, Docker, and JobsTracker dependencies\n   - Test that methods from these dependencies can be called from within the E2ETesting plugin\n\n5. **Lifecycle Methods Test**:\n   - Verify the plugin can be started and stopped without errors\n   - Check that resources are properly initialized during start and cleaned up during stop",
      "status": "done",
      "dependencies": [],
      "priority": "high",
      "subtasks": [
