      "id": 18,
      "title": "Implement Docker-based Puppeteer Runtime Environment",
      "description": "Create a containerized environment for running Puppeteer tests in isolation, with proper dependency management and API integration following existing plugin patterns.",
      "details": "This task involves creating a complete Docker-based runtime for Puppeteer browser automation tests. The implementation should include:\n\n1. Create a Dockerfile that:\n   - Uses a Node.js base image (preferably Alpine-based for smaller size)\n   - Installs Chromium and all required dependencies for headless browser operation\n   - Configures proper user permissions to run Chrome securely\n   - Sets up necessary environment variables (NODE_PATH, etc.)\n\n2. Implement volume mounting configuration:\n   - Define mount points for test scripts and test data\n   - Configure persistent storage for test results and screenshots\n   - Ensure proper permissions for file I/O between host and container\n\n3. Develop Docker orchestration API methods:\n   - Create container lifecycle management functions (create, start, stop, remove)\n   - Implement test execution methods that follow the patterns in HttpX and Nmap plugins\n   - Add proper error handling and logging for container operations\n   - Include resource management (CPU/memory limits, cleanup of orphaned containers)\n\n4. Add configuration options:\n   - Browser launch parameters (headless mode, viewport size, etc.)\n   - Network configuration (proxy settings, custom headers)\n   - Timeout and retry mechanisms\n\nThe implementation should be modular and follow the existing plugin architecture patterns. All Docker commands should be properly abstracted behind a clean API interface.",
      "testStrategy": "Testing should verify both the Docker environment and the API integration:\n\n1. Docker environment tests:\n   - Verify the container builds successfully without errors\n   - Confirm Chromium launches properly inside the container\n   - Test that volume mounts work correctly for reading test files and writing results\n   - Validate that the container runs with appropriate security constraints\n\n2. API integration tests:\n   - Create unit tests for each API method (container creation, execution, cleanup)\n   - Test error handling by simulating various failure conditions (missing dependencies, network issues)\n   - Verify resource management by monitoring container resource usage during test execution\n   - Test parallel execution of multiple containers to ensure isolation\n\n3. End-to-end tests:\n   - Create a sample Puppeteer test script that exercises common browser automation tasks\n   - Verify the test runs successfully in the containerized environment\n   - Compare results with the same test running directly on the host to ensure consistency\n   - Measure performance metrics to ensure the containerized solution has acceptable overhead\n\nAll tests should be automated and integrated into the CI/CD pipeline.",
      "status": "pending",
