    {
      "id": 19,
      "title": "Implement PenPal.E2ETesting API Core Functionality",
      "description": "Develop the core API for PenPal.E2ETesting that enables plugins to register, execute, and manage end-to-end tests following established plugin patterns.",
      "details": "Create a new plugin called PenPal.E2ETesting with the following core functionality:\n\n1. Test Registration:\n   - Implement RegisterTest() method that accepts test metadata (name, description, category) and test function\n   - Implement RegisterTestSuite() for grouping related tests\n   - Store tests in a structured format that allows for easy retrieval and execution\n\n2. Test Execution:\n   - Implement RunTest() method that executes a single test by ID or name\n   - Implement RunTestSuite() to execute all tests in a specific suite\n   - Implement RunAllTests() to execute all registered tests\n   - Include parameters for timeout settings and execution options\n\n3. Test Management:\n   - Implement GetTests() to retrieve all registered tests\n   - Implement GetTestById() and GetTestsByCategory() for filtered retrieval\n   - Create methods for test result storage and retrieval\n\n4. Result Handling:\n   - Design a standardized test result object structure\n   - Implement methods to store, retrieve, and analyze test results\n   - Include timestamps, execution time, pass/fail status, and error details\n\n5. Plugin Integration:\n   - Follow the established patterns from PenPal.Jobs and PenPal.HttpX\n   - Ensure proper dependency injection and service registration\n   - Implement appropriate interfaces for plugin discovery\n\nThe API should be designed for extensibility, allowing future enhancements like parallel test execution, conditional test runs, and integration with the UI.",
      "testStrategy": "1. Unit Tests:\n   - Create unit tests for each public method in the API\n   - Test RegisterTest() with valid and invalid inputs\n   - Verify GetTests() returns the correct collection of registered tests\n   - Test RunTest() with mocked test functions that pass, fail, and timeout\n\n2. Integration Tests:\n   - Create a test plugin that registers multiple test suites\n   - Verify that all registered tests can be retrieved correctly\n   - Execute test suites and verify results are stored properly\n   - Test error handling by deliberately causing test failures\n\n3. Edge Cases:\n   - Test behavior when executing non-existent tests\n   - Verify timeout handling for long-running tests\n   - Test concurrent test registration and execution\n   - Verify proper cleanup after test execution\n\n4. API Consistency:\n   - Review API against PenPal.Jobs and PenPal.HttpX to ensure consistent patterns\n   - Verify that dependency injection works correctly\n   - Ensure proper error messages are returned for all failure scenarios\n\nAll tests should be automated and included in the CI/CD pipeline to ensure ongoing functionality.",
      "status": "pending",
