    {
      "id": 20,
      "title": "Implement Core Test Execution Engine with Docker and Puppeteer Integration",
      "description": "Develop the central test execution engine that runs Puppeteer tests within Docker containers, manages the complete test lifecycle, and integrates with the JobsTracker for monitoring.",
      "details": "Create a modular test execution engine with the following components:\n\n1. **Container Management**:\n   - Implement Docker container creation, configuration, and cleanup\n   - Handle container networking and resource allocation\n   - Ensure proper isolation between test runs\n\n2. **Browser Lifecycle Management**:\n   - Initialize and configure Puppeteer browser instances\n   - Handle browser crashes and restarts\n   - Implement resource cleanup after test completion\n\n3. **Test Execution Flow**:\n   - Parse and validate test scripts/steps\n   - Execute test steps sequentially with proper error handling\n   - Implement timeout mechanisms for steps and overall test execution\n   - Support parallel test execution where appropriate\n\n4. **Artifact Collection**:\n   - Capture screenshots at configurable points (test start, end, failures)\n   - Collect browser console logs, network requests, and performance metrics\n   - Store artifacts with appropriate metadata for later analysis\n\n5. **Failure Handling**:\n   - Implement graceful error recovery mechanisms\n   - Provide detailed error reporting with context\n   - Support test retries with configurable attempts\n\n6. **JobsTracker Integration**:\n   - Report test progress in real-time\n   - Update test status (queued, running, completed, failed)\n   - Send execution metrics and timing information\n\n7. **Environment Management**:\n   - Implement setup and teardown hooks\n   - Support environment variable injection\n   - Handle test-specific configuration\n\nThe engine should be designed with extensibility in mind, allowing for future additions of different browser automation tools beyond Puppeteer.",
      "testStrategy": "Testing should be comprehensive and include:\n\n1. **Unit Tests**:\n   - Test each component in isolation with mocks for dependencies\n   - Verify proper error handling in each module\n   - Test configuration parsing and validation\n\n2. **Integration Tests**:\n   - Verify Docker container creation and management\n   - Test Puppeteer initialization and browser management\n   - Validate artifact collection and storage\n   - Test JobsTracker integration with mocked endpoints\n\n3. **End-to-End Tests**:\n   - Run sample test scripts through the complete execution pipeline\n   - Verify proper execution of multi-step test scenarios\n   - Test parallel execution capabilities\n   - Validate resource cleanup after test completion\n\n4. **Performance Tests**:\n   - Measure resource usage during test execution\n   - Test with varying loads to ensure scalability\n   - Benchmark startup and teardown times\n\n5. **Failure Scenario Tests**:\n   - Simulate browser crashes and verify recovery\n   - Test with intentionally failing test scripts\n   - Verify proper error reporting and retry mechanisms\n\nAll tests should be automated and included in the CI pipeline. Documentation should include examples of how to extend the engine for custom test scenarios.",
      "status": "pending",
