      "id": 21,
      "title": "Develop E2E Testing UI Interface Components",
      "description": "Build client-side components for an end-to-end testing interface that allows users to explore, execute, monitor, and view results of tests registered by plugins.",
      "details": "Create a comprehensive UI for E2E testing with the following components:\n\n1. Test Explorer:\n   - Implement a hierarchical view to display tests organized by plugin\n   - Include search/filter functionality to quickly find specific tests\n   - Add collapsible sections for better organization\n   - Show test metadata (estimated duration, last run status, etc.)\n\n2. Test Execution Controls:\n   - Create buttons for running selected tests, all tests, or specific test suites\n   - Implement test configuration options (environment selection, test parameters)\n   - Add ability to schedule test runs\n   - Include a cancel button for stopping test execution\n\n3. Live Progress Monitoring:\n   - Develop a real-time progress indicator showing overall completion percentage\n   - Display currently executing test with elapsed time\n   - Implement a log viewer that auto-scrolls with new entries\n   - Add visual indicators for test status (pending, running, passed, failed)\n\n4. Test Results Display:\n   - Create a summary view showing pass/fail counts and execution time\n   - Implement detailed view for individual test results\n   - Add ability to export results in various formats\n   - Include error details with stack traces for failed tests\n\nAll components should follow the existing Tester plugin UI patterns and integrate with the PenPal UI component system. Use responsive design principles to ensure the interface works well at different screen sizes. Implement proper error handling for API communication failures.",
      "testStrategy": "Testing should verify both the functionality and usability of the E2E testing interface:\n\n1. Component Testing:\n   - Verify each UI component renders correctly with different data inputs\n   - Test all interactive elements (buttons, dropdowns, etc.) respond appropriately\n   - Confirm components handle edge cases (empty test lists, long test names, etc.)\n\n2. Integration Testing:\n   - Verify the Test Explorer correctly displays tests from multiple plugins\n   - Confirm execution controls properly trigger test runs\n   - Test that progress monitoring accurately reflects test execution status\n   - Validate test results display matches actual test outcomes\n\n3. User Flow Testing:\n   - Complete end-to-end user journeys (find a test, run it, view results)\n   - Test keyboard navigation and accessibility features\n   - Verify responsive behavior at different viewport sizes\n\n4. Mock API Testing:\n   - Create mock API responses for various scenarios (success, failure, timeout)\n   - Verify UI handles API errors gracefully with appropriate user feedback\n\nUse Jest for component tests and Cypress for integration and user flow tests. Include visual regression tests to ensure UI consistency across browsers.",
