    {
      "id": 24,
      "title": "Implement Visual Regression Testing Framework",
      "description": "Develop and integrate a visual regression testing framework into the existing E2E testing system that can capture, compare, and report differences between screenshot baselines and current application state.",
      "details": "Implement a comprehensive visual regression testing solution with the following components:\n\n1. Screenshot Capture Mechanism:\n   - Create functions to capture full-page screenshots during test execution\n   - Support different viewport sizes and device emulation\n   - Implement waiting mechanisms to ensure page is fully rendered before capture\n\n2. Baseline Management System:\n   - Develop a storage solution for baseline images with proper versioning\n   - Create commands to generate/update baseline images\n   - Implement baseline organization by test case, viewport size, and environment\n\n3. Comparison Engine:\n   - Build an image comparison algorithm that can detect visual differences\n   - Support configurable threshold settings for difference sensitivity\n   - Implement pixel-by-pixel comparison with tolerance for anti-aliasing\n   - Add capability to ignore specified regions in screenshots\n\n4. Reporting System:\n   - Generate visual reports highlighting differences between baseline and current screenshots\n   - Create difference visualization with highlighted areas of change\n   - Include metrics on the percentage and nature of differences\n   - Integrate with existing test reporting infrastructure\n\n5. Test Framework Integration:\n   - Add custom commands/assertions to the E2E framework for visual testing\n   - Ensure compatibility with CI/CD pipeline\n   - Implement proper error handling and failure conditions\n\nTechnical Considerations:\n- Use a reliable image processing library compatible with the testing stack\n- Ensure the solution works across different environments (dev, staging, CI)\n- Optimize for performance to minimize impact on test execution time\n- Consider cross-browser compatibility issues",
      "testStrategy": "Verify the visual regression testing framework through the following test cases:\n\n1. Baseline Creation:\n   - Verify baseline images are correctly captured and stored\n   - Confirm proper organization of baselines by test, viewport, and environment\n   - Test the baseline update mechanism\n\n2. Comparison Accuracy:\n   - Create tests with known visual differences of varying magnitudes\n   - Verify the system correctly identifies differences above threshold\n   - Confirm the system ignores differences below threshold\n   - Test with different threshold configurations\n\n3. Region Exclusion:\n   - Verify the system correctly ignores specified regions\n   - Test with dynamic content areas excluded\n\n4. Cross-browser Compatibility:\n   - Verify consistent results across supported browsers\n   - Test with different viewport sizes and device emulations\n\n5. Reporting:\n   - Confirm difference reports are generated correctly\n   - Verify visual highlighting of differences is accurate\n   - Test integration with existing reporting systems\n\n6. Performance:\n   - Measure and establish baseline for performance impact\n   - Ensure large page screenshots don't cause memory issues\n\n7. Error Handling:\n   - Test behavior when baseline is missing\n   - Verify proper error messages when comparison fails\n   - Confirm graceful handling of corrupted images\n\nValidation should include both automated tests of the framework itself and manual verification of the visual reports and difference detection accuracy.",
      "status": "pending",
      "dependencies": [
