    {
      "id": 25,
      "title": "Implement Performance Monitoring Framework for E2E Tests",
      "description": "Develop and integrate a comprehensive performance monitoring framework into the existing E2E test suite that captures key metrics and enables performance assertions.",
      "details": "Create a modular performance monitoring framework that integrates with our E2E test infrastructure to measure and report on critical performance metrics. The implementation should include:\n\n1. **Page Load Time Measurement**:\n   - Track navigation timing API metrics (navigationStart, domContentLoaded, loadEvent)\n   - Implement custom markers for SPA route changes\n   - Calculate and store time-to-interactive metrics\n\n2. **Core Web Vitals Tracking**:\n   - Implement collection of LCP (Largest Contentful Paint)\n   - Track FID (First Input Delay) or its lab equivalent TBT (Total Blocking Time)\n   - Measure CLS (Cumulative Layout Shift)\n   - Capture INP (Interaction to Next Paint) where applicable\n\n3. **Memory Usage Monitoring**:\n   - Track JS heap size before and after key user flows\n   - Monitor for memory leaks during long-running tests\n   - Implement garbage collection forcing when needed for consistent measurements\n\n4. **Network Performance Analysis**:\n   - Capture request counts, sizes, and timing information\n   - Track API response times for critical endpoints\n   - Monitor for unnecessary network requests\n\n5. **Assertion Capabilities**:\n   - Create a flexible API for asserting performance thresholds\n   - Support both absolute thresholds and relative degradation checks\n   - Implement conditional test failures based on performance criteria\n\n6. **Reporting Infrastructure**:\n   - Store metrics in a structured format (JSON)\n   - Enable trend analysis across test runs\n   - Provide visualization capabilities or integration with existing dashboards\n\nThe framework should be configurable to run in different modes (basic/comprehensive) and should have minimal impact on the test execution time itself. Ensure backward compatibility with existing tests.",
      "testStrategy": "The implementation should be verified through the following test approach:\n\n1. **Unit Tests**:\n   - Create unit tests for each metric collection function\n   - Verify threshold calculation logic works correctly\n   - Test reporting format generation\n\n2. **Integration Tests**:\n   - Create a sample application with known performance characteristics\n   - Verify all metrics are collected accurately against this reference app\n   - Test the framework with both passing and failing performance thresholds\n\n3. **Validation Tests**:\n   - Compare metrics collected by the framework against browser DevTools measurements\n   - Verify Core Web Vitals align with Lighthouse or similar tools\n   - Ensure memory measurements correlate with browser task manager values\n\n4. **Regression Testing**:\n   - Run the framework against existing E2E tests to ensure it doesn't break them\n   - Measure the overhead added by the performance monitoring\n   - Verify that results are consistent across multiple runs\n\n5. **Edge Cases**:\n   - Test behavior during network throttling conditions\n   - Verify metrics collection during page errors or timeouts\n   - Test with various browser window sizes and device emulations\n\nAcceptance criteria should include documentation of the API, examples of usage in existing tests, and demonstration of a complete metrics collection and reporting cycle with visualizations of the results.",
      "status": "pending",
      "dependencies": [
        23
      ],
      "priority": "low"
    },
    {
      "id": 26,
      "title": "Develop E2E Test Recorder and Generator Tool",
      "description": "Create a browser-based tool that records user interactions and automatically generates executable test scripts that integrate with the existing test registration system.",
      "details": "Implement a comprehensive test recording and generation solution with the following components:\n\n1. Browser Extension/Bookmarklet:\n   - Develop a browser extension (supporting Chrome, Firefox, and Edge) or bookmarklet that can be activated on any page\n   - Implement recording capabilities that capture DOM events (clicks, form inputs, navigation, etc.)\n   - Include ability to add assertions during recording (element visibility, text content, etc.)\n   - Provide pause/resume/stop controls and visual indication of recording status\n   - Allow annotation of steps with custom descriptions\n\n2. Test Script Generator:\n   - Convert recorded actions into executable test code in a standard format (e.g., Cypress, Playwright, or TestCafe)\n   - Generate human-readable test scripts with appropriate selectors (preferring data-testid, aria attributes, then CSS selectors)\n   - Include timing configurations and wait statements for asynchronous operations\n   - Support parameterization of tests (extracting variables for data-driven testing)\n   - Implement smart selector generation that's resilient to UI changes\n\n3. Test Registration Integration:\n   - Create an API client that communicates with the existing test registration system\n   - Automatically register generated tests in the test catalog\n   - Support test metadata tagging (feature area, test type, priority)\n   - Implement version control integration to commit generated tests to repository\n\n4. User Interface:\n   - Design an intuitive UI for reviewing and editing recorded tests\n   - Provide options to customize generated code\n   - Include test preview functionality\n   - Support batch export of multiple recorded tests\n\nThe solution should be lightweight, require minimal setup, and produce tests that follow team coding standards and best practices.",
      "testStrategy": "Verify the implementation through the following test approach:\n\n1. Functional Testing:\n   - Record interactions on 5 different types of pages (static content, forms, dynamic content, SPAs, and multi-page flows)\n   - Verify that all user interactions are correctly captured (clicks, typing, selections, drag-drop, etc.)\n   - Confirm generated test scripts run successfully and reproduce the recorded actions\n   - Test across multiple browsers (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge)\n\n2. Integration Testing:\n   - Verify seamless integration with the test registration system\n   - Confirm that generated tests are properly registered with correct metadata\n   - Test version control integration by verifying commits of generated tests\n\n3. Usability Testing:\n   - Conduct sessions with 5+ developers to assess tool usability\n   - Measure time saved compared to manual test writing (target: 70% reduction)\n   - Collect feedback on UI intuitiveness and feature completeness\n\n4. Edge Cases:\n   - Test with iframes, shadow DOM, and dynamically generated content\n   - Verify handling of timeouts and loading states\n   - Test with very long sequences (100+ steps)\n   - Confirm behavior with network interruptions during recording\n\n5. Performance Testing:\n   - Measure overhead of recording tool on page performance (should be <5% impact)\n   - Test generation speed for large recordings (should complete in <10 seconds)\n\nAcceptance Criteria: The tool successfully records a complex user journey, generates a working test script that passes when executed, and properly registers the test in the test registration system, all within 5 minutes of developer time.",
